  ('SSC 462', 'Soil Fertility, Soil and Water Management', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', false),
  ('ABE 412', 'Agricultural Engineering Practical', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', false),
  ('FVM 433', 'Animal Health and Management', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', false),
  ('CSC 511', 'Field Experimentation and Data Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Design and management of experiments with crops. Randomized block, factorial and split plot designs; confounding; simple linear regressions. Data processing from commonly used designs and data interpretation. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options (Crop Production, Crop Protection, Horticulture).', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 521', 'Field Crops', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Classification of cereals and legumes. Centre of origin, history and importance, climatic and soil requirements, rotation and cropping sequences. Cultural operations: planting, management, harvesting, handling and storage of major cereals and legumes including rice, maize, guinea corn, millet, cowpea and groundnuts. Classification of roots and tubers, and of oil, drug and fibre crops, with their cultural operations. Pests and diseases of these crops and their control. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 531', 'Plant Protection', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'The concept and importance of crop protection against diseases. General classification of disease causal organisms and types of plant diseases. Principles of disease control including eradication, protection, exclusion and immunization. Pests: general introduction to major plant pests including insects, nematodes, birds and rodents; pests of major importance in Nigerian agriculture; survey of pest control techniques. Weeds: economic importance of weeds in tropical crop production; weed biology; methods of weed control. Fifth-year option course. Listed by the Crop Production and Crop Protection options. The Horticulture option table also lists code CSC 531 but titles it "Field Crops", duplicating CSC 521 - an inconsistency in the source page.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 541', 'Vegetable Crops', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Origin and classification of vegetable crops. Vegetable seeds - structure and functions of parts; seed viability, vigour, dormancy and methods of breaking seed dormancy. Types of vegetable growing. Factors affecting vegetable growing and distribution. Land preparation, nursery practices, manures, fertilizers and pesticides used in vegetable production. Vegetable seed production. Harvesting, processing and storage of vegetable crops. Crop rotation in vegetable growing. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options (the Horticulture table shortens the title to "Vegetable").', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 533', 'Economic Entomology', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'General classification of insects of economic importance. Life cycle and food habits of insects as basis of control measures. Problems of insects on growing crops and in storage. Insects as vectors of certain viral, bacterial and fungal diseases. Methods of insect pest control. Use of insecticides, methods of application and handling, phytotoxicity and mammalian toxicity. Economic considerations. Fifth-year option course. Listed by the Crop Production and Crop Protection options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 543', 'Plant Propagation', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Sexual propagation: media for seed propagation; seed germination requirements; seed storage and longevity; seed certification and quality control; quarantine regulations. Vegetative propagation: anatomical and physiological aspects of grafting and rooting; clones, sports and chimera; root-stock and scion interactions; role of the environment on vegetative propagation; growth regulators in plant propagation; budwood certification and maintenance of clonal gardens. Fifth-year option course. Listed by the Horticulture option only.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('SSC 531', 'Soil Survey and Land Use Planning', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('SSC 541', 'Soil Physics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by the Crop Production and Horticulture options. The Crop Protection option lists the same slot as "ANS 541 Soil Physic", an Animal Science code - an inconsistency in the source page.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('SSC 561', 'Soil Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('SSC 562', 'Soil and Plant Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'first', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by the Crop Production and Horticulture options. The Crop Protection option gives this slot as SSC 563, which elsewhere is Soil Fertility - an inconsistency in the source page.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 512', 'Plant Nutrition', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 1, 'The nutrient requirements of crops; influence of soil conditions and cation relationships on nutrient availability and uptake; movement and utilization of the major and micro-nutrients by crops; manures, fertilizers and limes; nutrient deficiency symptoms in crops and their remedies. Crop responses to nutrient application. The role of legumes. Plant sampling and sample preparation. Analysis of plant samples for major elements and the interpretation of data. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options. The course-description section gives this as 2 units while every option table gives 1 unit; the tables are used because they are what the printed 18-unit totals reconcile against.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 522', 'Forage and Fodder Crops', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 524', 'Plant Breeding and Genetics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Genetic principles as basis of plant breeding. Survey of objectives, methods and techniques of plant breeding. Germplasm bank. Reproductive systems in plants and their role in plant breeding. Application of breeding methods to the improvement of self-pollinated, cross-pollinated and sexually reproduced crops. Development and maintenance of breeding stock, multiplication and distribution of improved crop varieties. Breeding for pest and disease control. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 534', 'Weed Science', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Biology of weeds. Principles and methods of weed control. Classification, chemistry, selectivity, formulation, application and mode of action of herbicides. Herbicide-environment interaction. Safety factors in the use of herbicides. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 542', 'Plantation Crops', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Origin, distribution and importance of tropical plantation crops. Climatic and soil requirements, cultural operations, methods of propagation, nursery practices, plantation management, harvesting, processing and storage of major plantation crops including oil palm, rubber, cocoa, coffee, kola, cashew, banana/plantain, sugar cane, tea and sisal hemp. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 544', 'Post Harvest Physiology and Product Storage', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Storage life of harvested fruits, vegetables and flowers. Tropical environment in relation to maturity, ripeness and senescence including climacteric. Physical and chemical indices of quality in fruit and vegetable crops. Controlled environment for transit and long-term storage. Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('CSC 552', 'Special Project', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 4, 'Fifth-year option course. The Crop Production option gives the project as CSC 552; the Crop Protection and Horticulture tables give CSC 592 and the course-description section gives CSC 572. All three refer to the same 4-unit final-year project - the source page is inconsistent about its code.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
  ('SSC 542', 'Principles of Irrigation and Drainage', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Agriculture', 'Crop Science', '500 Level', 'second', 2, 'Fifth-year option course. Listed by all three options.', '[]'::jsonb, 'UNN Department of Crop Science official website', true),
